WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.992 --> 00:00:15.881
Ally held her breath.

2
00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:21.725
Julius' phone rang once, twice, then "Hey, Mateo!"

3
00:00:21.985 --> 00:00:22.726
Julius said.

4
00:00:22.746 --> 00:00:25.488
"You reached me while I was reading a good spy novel.

5
00:00:25.708 --> 00:00:28.110
What's up?"

6
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:31.372
"Uh Ally fumbled to read the script on Alpha's screen.

7
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:32.901
"Hello, Julius.

8
00:00:33.241 --> 00:00:38.725
This is Allyzooba of Astralia, east of the Milky Her voice trailed off.

9
00:00:38.745 --> 00:00:41.908
"Eek! Alpha's script is terrible!"

10
00:00:42.388 --> 00:00:42.929
Ally thought.

11
00:00:42.949 --> 00:00:46.332
"Ally?" Julius sounded concerned.

12
00:00:46.352 --> 00:00:50.415
"Are you okay?"

13
00:00:50.435 --> 00:00:55.459
"I, er I was wondering if you'd want to Ally flushed.

14
00:00:55.479 --> 00:00:57.961
"I mean you don't have to, no pressure.

15
00:00:58.882 --> 00:01:00.944
Oh, maybe this was a bad idea.

16
00:01:01.532 --> 00:01:03.133
I bet you were just being nice, right?"

17
00:01:03.153 --> 00:01:05.795
"Nice about what?"

18
00:01:06.175 --> 00:01:07.035
Julius asked.

19
00:01:07.996 --> 00:01:09.517
"About going on a date."

20
00:01:10.017 --> 00:01:12.858
Ally paused, and then added, "With me."

21
00:01:13.799 --> 00:01:15.060
There was a long silence.

22
00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.461
Ally started to sweat.

23
00:01:17.481 --> 00:01:20.683
"I knew it was a bad idea to ask you!"

24
00:01:20.703 --> 00:01:21.924
"Not at all!"

25
00:01:22.244 --> 00:01:22.984
Julius said.

26
00:01:23.004 --> 00:01:25.646
"I'm sorry, I just didn't know what to say.

27
00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.727
I've been trying to call you.

28
00:01:27.807 --> 00:01:29.488
But you haven't answered my calls.

29
00:01:30.232 --> 00:01:31.672
I thought you didn't want to talk to me."

30
00:01:32.893 --> 00:01:40.035
"Really? I Ally looked down at Alpha and guessed what had happened—Alpha still wasn't working right.

31
00:01:40.055 --> 00:01:43.376
"I'm sorry," she said.

32
00:01:43.396 --> 00:01:47.557
"My phone is, er, unreliable."

33
00:01:47.577 --> 00:01:51.078
"I understand," Julius said.

34
00:01:51.098 --> 00:01:53.759
"Anyway, I'd love to go a date with you."

35
00:01:54.719 --> 00:01:55.379
"You would?"

36
00:01:55.959 --> 00:01:56.660
Ally smiled.

37
00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:58.100
"That's great!

38
00:01:58.824 --> 00:02:02.987
Mateo suggested that we go on a double date to watch the eclipse on Saturday night."

39
00:02:03.007 --> 00:02:05.989
"That sounds cool," Julius said.

40
00:02:06.809 --> 00:02:08.070
"Should we meet in the park at seven?"

41
00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:10.512
"Yes! See you then!"

42
00:02:11.032 --> 00:02:12.113
Ally hung up the phone.

43
00:02:12.853 --> 00:02:16.836
She was so happy, she didn't even feel mad at Alpha for messing up the script.

44
00:02:16.856 --> 00:02:19.678
"Alpha, play some music.

45
00:02:20.118 --> 00:02:21.079
I want to dance!"

46
00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:25.482
"Harumph!" Alpha snorted and shut herself off.

47
00:02:27.543 --> 00:02:28.404
Ally shook her head.

48
00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:31.901
"Alpha's acting so weird," she thought.

49
00:02:31.921 --> 00:02:35.562
"Almost as if she doesn't like Julius or something.

50
00:02:35.582 --> 00:02:39.203
Hmm. Can computers get jealous?"

51
00:02:42.544 --> 00:02:47.225
The next day Ally was working at the counter while Flo was in the kitchen helping Randy.

52
00:02:48.105 --> 00:02:49.166
Barry rushed over.

53
00:02:49.186 --> 00:02:52.506
"I know what to serve for the food truck contest!

54
00:02:53.247 --> 00:02:55.407
I bet no one else will have it at their truck!"

55
00:02:56.307 --> 00:02:56.908
"What is it?"

56
00:02:58.488 --> 00:02:58.728
Ally said.

57
00:02:58.748 --> 00:02:59.849
"It's a surprise!"

58
00:03:00.169 --> 00:03:00.729
Barry said.

59
00:03:00.749 --> 00:03:03.250
"I'm going into the kitchen now to try it out."

60
00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:06.771
"I can't wait to see what it is," Ally said.

61
00:03:11.053 --> 00:03:13.154
Two customers came in and sat at the counter.

62
00:03:13.174 --> 00:03:16.275
"Can I get you something to drink?"

63
00:03:16.675 --> 00:03:18.496
Ally asked, handing them menus.

64
00:03:19.917 --> 00:03:21.797
"We're not here to eat," the man said.

65
00:03:21.817 --> 00:03:23.378
"I'm Jerry.

66
00:03:23.578 --> 00:03:25.499
I'm a producer at Food Truck Rally.

67
00:03:26.459 --> 00:03:29.600
This is Sally, my cameraperson."

68
00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:31.902
"Oh!" Ally smoothed her hair.

69
00:03:31.922 --> 00:03:34.043
"Am I on TV now?"

70
00:03:35.985 --> 00:03:37.005
"Not yet."

71
00:03:37.386 --> 00:03:38.106
Jerry laughed.

72
00:03:38.126 --> 00:03:39.987
"Is Barry here?"

73
00:03:40.007 --> 00:03:41.989
"He's in the kitchen.

74
00:03:42.769 --> 00:03:45.871
In fact, he's trying out a new recipe for the contest."

75
00:03:46.792 --> 00:03:48.253
"Oh, good," Jerry said.

76
00:03:49.093 --> 00:03:53.276
"We want to get footage of all the food truck teams in the days leading up to the

77
00:03:53.316 --> 00:03:58.380
contest. You contestants signed legal forms to participate in the contest.

78
00:03:59.396 --> 00:04:01.558
But we need everyone to fill out another form.

79
00:04:01.999 --> 00:04:03.860
Can you ask the others to come out of the kitchen?"

80
00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:07.203
"Sure! I'll get Barry, Randy, and Flo."

81
00:04:09.045 --> 00:04:10.766
Randy and Barry came out first.

82
00:04:13.409 --> 00:04:15.110
Jerry handed out sheets of paper.

83
00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:17.573
"Here are the waivers for you to sign."

84
00:04:18.794 --> 00:04:20.675
Ally, Randy, and Barry signed them.

85
00:04:22.617 --> 00:04:23.878
"Great!" Jerry said.

86
00:04:23.898 --> 00:04:25.700
"Now we can film you.

87
00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.702
Barry, can you tell the camera what you're working on?"

88
00:04:31.303 --> 00:04:35.006
"Well, I was going to keep it a surprise, but I suppose I can reveal it to the

89
00:04:35.046 --> 00:04:36.668
camera." Barry smiled.

90
00:04:36.688 --> 00:04:40.331
"I call it my Out of This World Cosmic Club.

91
00:04:41.011 --> 00:04:45.275
It's turkey and avocado, topped by huevos rancheros and potato chips."

92
00:04:45.295 --> 00:04:48.237
"That sounds like a winner to me!"

93
00:04:48.637 --> 00:04:49.138
Ally said.

94
00:04:49.158 --> 00:04:50.919
"What's a winner?"

95
00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:53.301
Flo asked as she came out of the kitchen.

96
00:04:53.321 --> 00:04:56.464
"Barry's sandwich for the contest," Ally said.

97
00:04:57.272 --> 00:05:01.316
"Here, Flo, you have to sign a waiver so the TV show can film you working."

98
00:05:01.336 --> 00:05:03.057
"Oh no!"

99
00:05:03.758 --> 00:05:06.820
Flo's cheeks flushed as she covered her face with a menu.

100
00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:08.942
"I don't want to be on TV!"

101
00:05:08.962 --> 00:05:11.924
"Really?" Ally was surprised.

102
00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:16.548
She thought everybody on Earth loved the idea of being on TV and becoming famous.

103
00:05:16.568 --> 00:05:21.352
"But you like to sing and make jokes and—" "I said no!"

104
00:05:21.813 --> 00:05:25.396
Flo scurried back into the kitchen with the menu still covering her face.

105
00:05:26.412 --> 00:05:29.637
"That was strange," Ally thought, confused.

106
00:05:30.919 --> 00:05:36.367
She tried to read Flo's mind, but she could only hear one thought from Flo: "Get me out

107
00:05:36.387 --> 00:05:38.150
of here as fast as possible!"
